}\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\nAUC: 0.8869\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Pathological Example 1\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#1516e5e5 .cell execution_count=10}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-11-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#1995c9be .cell execution_count=11}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-12-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n## Pathological Example 1 {.smaller}\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#65fb9582 .cell execution_count=12}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-13-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#668d49ca .cell execution_count=13}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-14-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n$$\\text{Sensitivity} = \\frac{TP}{TP + FN} = \\frac{\\text{Positives Above Line}}{\\text{All Positives}} = \\frac{100}{100} = 1$$\n$$1-\\text{Specificity} = 1-\\frac{TN}{TN + FP} = \\frac{FP}{TN + FP} = \\frac{\\text{Negatives Above Line}}{\\text{All Negatives}} = \\frac{100}{100} = 1$$\n\n## Pathological Example 1 {.smaller}\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#674b84ad .cell execution_count=14}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-15-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#57f6a590 .cell execution_count=15}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-16-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n$$\\text{Sensitivity} = \\frac{100}{100} = 1$$\n$$1-\\text{Specificity} = \\frac{\\text{Negatives Above Line}}{100} \\approx 0.5$$\n\n## Pathological Example 1 {.smaller}\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#8dad080c .cell execution_count=16}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-17-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#04cb4019 .cell execution_count=17}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-18-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n$$\\text{Sensitivity} = \\frac{100}{100} = 1$$\n$$1-\\text{Specificity} = \\frac{0}{100} = 0$$\n\n## Pathological Example 2\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#e5f0c33d .cell execution_count=18}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-19-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#bae752b7 .cell execution_count=19}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-20-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n## Pathological Example 3\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#d957b873 .cell execution_count=20}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-21-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#83ad5dee .cell execution_count=21}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-22-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n## Pathological Example 4\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#c6c8a42f .cell execution_count=22}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-23-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#75524671 .cell execution_count=23}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-24-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n## Pathological Example 5\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#86a1cbc5 .cell execution_count=24}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-25-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#9bc7fe6b .cell execution_count=25}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-26-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n## Pathological Example 6\n\n:::: columns\n:::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n\n::: {#46193a3d .cell execution_count=26}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-27-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {#bef075e6 .cell execution_count=27}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![](10-roc-auc_files/figure-revealjs/cell-28-output-1.png){}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n::::\n\n## AUC Questions\n\n-   What should be the minimum AUC?\n-   What should be that maximum possible AUC?\n\n# Review of Classification Metrics\n\n## Review: Logistic Regression vs KNN {.smaller}\n\n- Logistic regression $\\implies$ parametric , KNN $\\implies$ non-parametric.\n- Logistic regression $\\implies$ only for classification problems ($Y$ categorical), KNN $\\implies$ both regression and classification.\n- Logistic regression is (more) interpretable, KNN is not.\n- Logistic regression allows qualitative predictors. Euclidean distance with KNN does not allow for qualitative predictors.\n- Prediction: KNN can be pretty good for small $p$, that is, $p \\le 4$ and large $n$. Performance of KNN deteriorates as $p$ increases - curse of dimensionality.\n\n## Classification Metrics App {.smaller}\n\n-   Dr. F will split you into four groups\n-   On one of your computers connect to a tv and [open this app](https://efriedlander.shinyapps.io/ClassificationMetrics/)\n-   Do the following based on your group number:\n    +   1: Choose plane on the first screen\n    +   2: Choose circle on the first screen\n    +   3: Choose parabola on the first screen\n    +   4: Choose sine curve on the first screen\n-   We will generate data from this population... do you think KNN or logistic regression will yield a better classifier? Why?\n\n## Classification Metrics App {.smaller}\n\n-   On the second tab generate a small test and training set\n-   On the third tab fit a KNN model with 5 neighbors and then a logistic regression model\n-   Which model do you think will perform better based on the plots you see?\n-   Choose the better model, click fit, and click on the fourth tab\n\n## Questions\n\nUsing the app, try and answer the following questions:\n\n- Which of the metrics are most and least impacted by:\n  - Sample size\n  - Imbalanced data (i.e. proportion positive near 0 or 1)\n  - High noise\n\n",
